<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/c2012a00169-sch-3-sec-4-ss-2-logic-deontic-1> a <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/LogicApplication>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/modality> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Deontic>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/operator> "Permit";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Permission to appeal to a designated court.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(a) the person may appeal to the designated court against an objection decision under that Act (the ACNC objection decision); and (b) the objection decision mentioned in subsection (1) (the taxation objection decision) and the ACNC objection decision are related, or it would be efficient for the designated court to consider the decisions together.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "(2) Treat a reference in subsection (1) to appealing to the Federal Court as being a reference to appealing to a designated court (within the meaning of the Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012)";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/executionSurface> "modalities::logic::deontic";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/confidence> 1.0000;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/c2012a00169-sch-3-sec-4-ss-2> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/asserts> <https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/c2012a00169-sch-3-sec-4-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2>.
